WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.502
Path traversal prevention in Python protects file operations from
untrusted path influence.

2
00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:14.649
The central design principle is simple: users should not directly control
where the application reads, writes, serves, deletes, extracts, or copies
files.

3
00:00:14.649 --> 00:00:25.585
Python code should treat filenames, path parameters, upload metadata,
archive entries, database-stored references, and generated file names
according to their source and trust level.

4
00:00:25.585 --> 00:00:40.853
Strong designs use trusted base directories, path-aware APIs,
canonicalization, base-directory containment checks, opaque identifiers,
allowlisted storage records, generated storage names, and clear separation
between display names and storage names.

5
00:00:40.853 --> 00:00:52.545
They also enforce authorization before file access, protect tenant
boundaries, use framework and storage helpers deliberately, and avoid
leaking internal paths through responses, logs, or errors.

6
00:00:52.545 --> 00:00:55.984
File safety depends on environment details as well as code.

7
00:00:55.984 --> 00:01:07.882
Operating system behavior, symbolic links, archive formats, temporary
files, mounted volumes, containers, serverless runtimes, object storage
keys, proxies, and web servers can all affect outcomes.

8
00:01:07.882 --> 00:01:13.178
A design that is safe in one deployment can become fragile if assumptions
are undocumented.

9
00:01:13.178 --> 00:01:18.061
File workflows should be explicit enough to review and test as the
platform changes.

10
00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:22.669
The goal is predictable, authorized, auditable, and constrained file
access.

11
00:01:22.669 --> 00:01:30.234
Good prevention reduces the chance of exposing private files, secrets,
logs, source code, customer data, or internal artifacts.

12
00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:33.811
It also makes incidents easier to investigate and remediate.

13
00:01:33.811 --> 00:01:41.720
Treat file access as a security boundary, not a convenience string
operation, and the application becomes safer and easier to maintain.
